person_id":"tvfy_10044","person_slug":"simon-birmingham","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Fielding","party":"Family First","person_id":"tvfy_10221","person_slug":"steve-fielding","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Hutchins","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10323","person_slug":"steve-hutchins","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Boyce","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10062","person_slug":"sue-boyce","vote":"no"},{"name":"Trish Crossin","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10161","person_slug":"trish-crossin","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ursula Stephens","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10609","person_slug":"ursula-stephens","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Fair Work Bill 2008 — In Committee","noes":29,"question":"Consideration resumed. Guy Barnett The committee is considering government amendment (2) on sheet RE403. Steve Fielding I was talking to this before the break. This is about inserting terms for long-distance transport workers. I was saying that I could not see a recommendation on this issue in the Senate Standing Committee on Education, Employment and Workplace Relations report on the Fair Work Bill 2008 provisions. Obviously this is a fairly contentious issue and there has been a fair bit of press about the blue-card system in New South Wales. By the same token, you want to make sure that there is safety and security on our roads as far as long-distance transport goes. Considering it is such a contentious issue, I strongly suggest to the committee that we send to a committee a reference—which I foreshadow—for amendment (2) to be looked at and well considered before we go about inserting it at the eleventh hour tonight. I think there are two views that need to be put forward strongly. We have heard the cases from the government and the opposition. We could spend a lot of time here continuing that debate, but I think the best way of resolving this is to send this particular amendment to a committee to be looked at and to have them report back to the Senate. Eric Abetz There are still some issues at large in relation to this amendment. The first one, of course, is why the transport industry was not consulted but the Transport Workers Union was. The other issue is why this was not part of the original framework. The reason it was not part of the original framework, I suggest to the minister, is that under award modernisation we were going to have a framework that covered all awards but with this amendment we are carving out certain elements peculiar to the transport industry to give a huge leg-up to the Transport Workers Union in the terms described by Senator Williams before the dinner adjournment. In this, we understand that safety is going to become an issue in the ","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-1641","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2009-03-19/8"}
